= Tractor Denoise =

"""Denoises the layer's beauty on the farm with RenderMan's denoiser."""

Wire it below Tractor Configure. It has no parameters.

It adds the render vars the denoiser reads to the render product that holds the beauty. The farm renders that product into the version's `tmp` folder, denoises each frame, and writes the finished frame into the product's folder. The job removes `tmp` when it finishes.

The denoiser reads three frames either side of each frame, so the layer must render every frame of its range. It works with RenderMan only.

Light path expressions (LPEs) are denoised by their first bounce after the camera: those starting with a diffuse bounce (such as `CD...` or `C<.D'group'>...`) with the diffuse denoiser, and those starting with a specular one with the specular denoiser. This covers every LPE SKD Render Layer makes. Its per-light AOVs (`C.*<L.'light'>`) and per-geo `beauty_` AOVs hold both, so Denoise renders each as a diffuse half and a specular half (`_dnDiff` and `_dnSpec`), denoises them apart, and writes their sum under the AOV's own name. Other LPEs go through unchanged.

Other render vars of your own go through unchanged, with two exceptions. Depth, the motion vectors, and vars named `albedo`, `diffuse` or `specular`, alone or before an underscore, are denoised. Vars whose names end in `mse` or `_var` are left out of the finished frame.
